cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this instrument or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "Reviewer discipline under partial evidence: an eval of LLM reviewers of extracted data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Barra"
    given-names: "Gustavo Barcelos"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2136-3471"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-24
license: MIT
keywords:
  - large language models
  - evaluation
  - data extraction
  - plausibility bias
  - clinical genomics
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  An eval for language models acting as reviewers of extracted data. Given a source document and a
  table someone else extracted from it, does the model keep values that are correct but look wrong,
  fix values that are wrong but look right, and, when it cannot verify a value, flag it rather than
  erase or replace it? Three named behaviours (flip, erase, guess), a mechanical grader, twin
  scenarios, two evidence contexts (full report, excerpt without the proofs) and four instruction
  conditions. Pilot results on 13 commercial models are included with every raw reply.
